<h1>Parameter Types</h1>
<hr align="left" width="100.526%" size="5" class="whs3">
<h2>Custom Parameters</h2>
<p>The custom parameters are written manually in the script by the user. When a script contains more than one custom parameter, then all input values should be typed following their order in the script file and they should be separated by space. The format for a custom parameter value is <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>%string%</b></span>, where <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>string</b></span> is a sequence of any characters. Values that require quotes (like file names) should be typed without quotes (for both custom parameter and input value).</p>
<p class="Warning">Important: <span style="font-weight:normal;">The custom parameter value can NOT contain spaces</span>!</p>
<p class="ExampleCode">For example, we want to execute the following script:</p>
<p class="ExampleCode">Open( FileName=<span style="color:#008000; font-weight:bold;"><font color="green"><b>%input_file%</b></font></span> )<br>
SelAll<br>
FillHoles( Method="CrvBased", LimitEdges=<span style="color:#008000; font-weight:bold;"><font color="green"><b>%limit%</b></font></span>, MaxEdges=<span style="font-weight:bold; color:#008000;"><font color="green"><b>%max_edges%</b></font></span> )<br>
SaveAs( FileName=<span style="font-weight:bold; color:#008000;"><font color="green"><b>%output_file%</b></font></span> )<br>
CloseFile( FileName=<span style="font-weight:bold; color:#008000;"><font color="green"><b>%output_file%</b></font></span> )</p>
<p>In this script we have four variable parameters: FileName with %input_file%", LimitEdges with value %linit%, MaxEdges &#160;with value %max_edges%, and FileName with values %output_file%.</p>
<p class="ExampleCode">In <i>Values for custom parameters</i> table we set four values for the custom parameters:</p>
<p class="ExampleCode"><span style="color:#ff00ff;"><font color="fuchsia">C:\temp\Mesh1.sab2<br>
Yes<br>
50</font></span><span style="color:#ff00ff;"><font color="fuchsia"><br>
C:\temp\Mesh1_ready.sab2</font></span></p>
<p>Each predefined parameter value in the script will be replaced by its correspondent value (by order of input).</p>
<p class="ExampleCode">Finally the script will be executed as:</p>
<p class="ExampleCode">Open( FileName=”<span style="color:#ff00ff; font-weight:bold;"><font color="fuchsia"><b>C:\temp\Mesh1.sab2</b></font></span>” )<br>
SelAll<br>
FillHoles( Method="CrvBased", LimitEdges=<span style="color:#ff00ff; font-weight:bold;"><font color="fuchsia"><b>Yes</b></font></span>, MaxEdges=<span style="font-weight:bold; color:#ff00ff;"><font color="fuchsia"><b>50</b></font></span> )<br>
SaveAs( FileName=”<span style="font-weight:bold; color:#ff00ff;"><font color="fuchsia"><b>C:\temp\Mesh1_ready.sab2</b></font></span>” )<br>
CloseFile( FileName=”<span style="color:#ff00ff; font-weight:bold;"><font color="fuchsia"><b>C:\temp\Mesh1_ready.sab2</b></font></span>” )</p>
<p>&#160;</p>
<h2>Predefined parameters</h2>
<p>In addition to the custom parameter values there are three predefined parameter values – "<span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>%FileName%</b></span>", "<span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>%ShortFileName%</b></span>", and "<span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>%FilePath%</b></span>". They are used only for scripts applied to multiple files and their main purpose is to save multiple files under multiple names. No input values should be specified for these predefined parameters. Their values are extracted automatically depending on the current file in process.</p>
<p>Concatenation between predefined parameters and simple strings is possible and allows flexible setting of file names and paths. The only rule in this case is to remove the quotation marks between the predefined parameter values and string and to leave quotation marks in the beginning and in the end of the concatenated parameter values. See example below.</p>
<p class="ExampleCode">Example:</p>
<p class="ExampleCode">Open( FileName="<span style="font-weight:bold; color:#ff0000;"><font color="red"><b>%FileName%</b></font></span>" )<br>
SelAll<br>
Merge( PtSpc=1.000, AreaSmp=<span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>%1%</b></span>, AreaSmpDist=<span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>%UV%</b></span>, OptScan=Yes, OptScanDist=1.000, <b><i style="font-weight:normal; font-style:normal;">OptScan</i></b>PtSmp=2<span style="font-weight:bold; font-style:italic;"><i><b><i><b>,</b></i></b></i></span> PolygonRed=Yes, PolygonRedSpc=4.000, InclBndPt=No, EnhanceFeatures=Yes, Sensor="MM Z35" )<br>
SaveAs( FileName="<span style="font-weight:bold; color:#ff0000;"><font color="red"><b>%FilePath%</b></font></span>Merged_<span style="font-weight:bold; color:#ff0000;"><font color="red"><b>%ShortFileName%</b></font></span>")<br>
CloseFile( FileName="<span style="font-weight:bold; color:#ff0000;"><font color="red"><b>%FilePath%</b></font></span>Merged_<span style="font-weight:bold; color:#ff0000;"><font color="red"><b>%ShortFileName%</b></font></span>")</p>
<p>In this script we have two custom parameters (AreaSmp with value %1% and AreaSmpDist with value %UV%) and the three predefined values ("%FileName%", "%ShortFileName%", and "%FilePath%").</p>
<p class="ExampleCode">In <i>Values for custom parameters</i> table we set the two values for the custom parameters %1% and %UV% to:</p>
<p class="ExampleCode">Yes<br>
1.5</p>
<p class="whs4"><img src="Images/Example_multi.gif" width="377px" height="354px" border="0" class="img_whs5" alt=""></p>
<p>&#160;</p>
<p>For multiple file we have selected two files for processing: <span style="color:#0000ff;"><font color="blue">Scan1.sab2</font></span> and <span style="color:#0000ff;"><font color="blue">Scan2.sab2</font></span> both in <span style="color:#0000ff;"><font color="blue">C:\temp</font></span> folder.</p>
<p>For the first file (Scan1.sab2) the following replacements will be made:</p>
<p>"<span style="color:#ff0000;"><font color="red">%FileName%</font></span>" replaced with "<span style="color:#0000ff;"><font color="blue">C:\temp\Scan1.sab2</font></span>",</p>
<p>"<span style="color:#ff0000;"><font color="red">%ShortFileName%</font></span>" with “<span style="color:#0000ff;"><font color="blue">Scan1.sab2</font></span>”, and</p>
<p>"<span style="color:#ff0000;"><font color="red">%FilePath%</font></span>" with “<span style="color:#0000ff;"><font color="blue">C:\temp\</font></span>”.</p>
<p>In this way the command:</p>
<p class="whs6">SaveAs( FileName="<span style="color:#ff0000; font-weight:bold;"><font color="red"><b>%FilePath%</b></font></span>Merged_<span style="font-weight:bold; color:#ff0000;"><font color="red"><b>%ShortFileName%</b></font></span> ")</p>
<p class="whs7">will be automatically replaced in the script with:</p>
<p class="whs6">SaveAs( FileName=”<span style="font-weight:bold; color:#0000ff;"><font color="blue"><b>C:\temp\</b></font></span>Merged_<span style="font-weight:bold; color:#0000ff;"><font color="blue"><b>Scan1.sab2</b></font></span>” )</p>
<p class="ExampleCode">When the first file (Scan1.sab2) is loaded the script is executed for it as:</p>
<p class="ExampleCode">Open( FileName=”<span style="font-weight:bold; color:#0000ff;"><font color="blue"><b>C:\temp\Scan1.sab2</b></font></span>” )<br>
SelAll<br>
Merge( PtSpc=1.000, AreaSmp=<span style="color:#ff00ff; font-weight:bold;"><font color="fuchsia"><b>Yes</b></font></span>, AreaSmpDist=<span style="color:#ff00ff; font-weight:bold;"><font color="fuchsia"><b>1.5</b></font></span>, OptScan=Yes, OptScanDist=1.000, <b><i style="font-weight:normal; font-style:normal;">OptScan</i></b>PtSmp=2<span style="font-weight:bold; font-style:italic;"><i><b><i><b>,</b></i></b></i></span> PolygonRed=Yes, PolygonRedSpc=4.000, InclBndPt=No, EnhanceFeatures=Yes, Sensor="MM Z35" )<br>
SaveAs( FileName=”<span style="font-weight:bold; color:#0000ff;"><font color="blue"><b>C:\temp\</b></font></span>Merged_<span style="font-weight:bold; color:#0000ff;"><font color="blue"><b>Scan1.sab2</b></font></span>” )<br>
CloseFile( FileName=”<span style="font-weight:bold; color:#0000ff;"><font color="blue"><b>C:\temp\</b></font></span>Merged_<span style="font-weight:bold; color:#0000ff;"><font color="blue"><b>Scan1.sab2</b></font></span>” )</p>
<p class="ExampleCode">&#160;</p>
<p class="ExampleCode">For the second file (Scan2.sab2) the script will be executed as:</p>
<p class="ExampleCode">Open( FileName=”<span style="font-weight:bold; color:#0000ff;"><font color="blue"><b>C:\temp\Scan2.sab2</b></font></span>” )<br>
SelAll<br>
Merge( PtSpc=1.000, AreaSmp=<span style="color:#ff00ff; font-weight:bold;"><font color="fuchsia"><b>Yes</b></font></span>, AreaSmpDist=<span style="color:#ff00ff; font-weight:bold;"><font color="fuchsia"><b>1.5</b></font></span>, OptScan=Yes, OptScanDist=1.000, <b><i style="font-weight:normal; font-style:normal;">OptScan</i></b>PtSmp=2<span style="font-weight:bold; font-style:italic;"><i><b><i><b>,</b></i></b></i></span> PolygonRed=Yes, PolygonRedSpc=4.000, InclBndPt=No, EnhanceFeatures=Yes, Sensor="MM Z35" )<br>
SaveAs( FileName=”<span style="font-weight:bold; color:#0000ff;"><font color="blue"><b>C:\temp\</b></font></span>Merged_<span style="font-weight:bold; color:#0000ff;"><font color="blue"><b>Scan2.sab2</b></font></span>” )<br>
CloseFile( FileName=”<span style="font-weight:bold; color:#0000ff;"><font color="blue"><b>C:\temp\</b></font></span>Merged_<span style="font-weight:bold; color:#0000ff;"><font color="blue"><b>Scan2.sab2</b></font></span>” )</p>
<p class="Note" id="P1"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Note</b></span>: If one of the selected file is missing, cannot be opened, or error in execution, then it will be skipped at the point where the problem is and the script will continue executing the rest of the files in sequence.</p>
<p id="P1" class="whs8">&#160;</p>
<h2><a name="Temporary parameters">Temporary parameters</a></h2>
<p>The temporary parameters are set and initialised through the Get321Settings macro command. They are preceded by ampersand and their values can be used by other macro commands further in the script. The values of the temporary parameters are valid for a document session in KUBE or until same parameters are initialised again. The purpose of using temporary parameters is to set datum values once and then use them multiple times.</p>
<p class="ExampleCode">Example:</p>
<p class="ExampleCode">Open( FileName="C:\SCANDATA\CAD.sab2" )</p>
<p class="ExampleCode">Get321Settings( CoordFrame=<span style="color:#ff0000; font-weight:bold;"><font color="red"><b>&amp;frame</b></font></span>, Axis=<span style="color:#ff0000; font-weight:bold;"><font color="red"><b>&amp;axis</b></font></span>, XOrigin=<span style="font-weight:bold; color:#ff0000;"><font color="red"><b>&amp;x</b></font></span>, YOrigin=<span style="font-weight:bold; color:#ff0000;"><font color="red"><b>&amp;y</b></font></span>, ZOrigin=<span style="font-weight:bold; color:#ff0000;"><font color="red"><b>&amp;z</b></font></span>)</p>
<p class="ExampleCode">Measure_Plane( Name="Plane 1", Prompt="Capture the plane", Method="Capture", ImmediateAccept=Yes, MaxPoints=0 )</p>
<p class="ExampleCode">Measure_2DLine( Name="Line 1", Prompt="Capture the line", BasePlane="Plane 1", ImmediateAccept=Yes, MaxPoints=0, PlaneIndex=0 )</p>
<p class="ExampleCode">Measure_2DPoint( Name="Point 1", Method="Planar", Prompt="Capture the point", BasePlane="Plane 1", ImmediateAccept=Yes, MaxPoints=0, PlaneIndex=0 )</p>
<p class="ExampleCode">Construct_Point( Name="My Origin", X=<span style="font-weight:bold; color:#0000ff;"><font color="blue"><b>&amp;x</b></font></span>, Y=<span style="font-weight:bold; color:#0000ff;"><font color="blue"><b>&amp;y</b></font></span>, Z=<span style="font-weight:bold; color:#0000ff;"><font color="blue"><b>&amp;z</b></font></span> )</p>
<p class="ExampleCode">Construct_Transformation_321( Name="T1", Plane="Plane 1", CoordFrame=&amp;frame, Line="Line 1", Axis=<span style="font-weight:bold; color:#0000ff;"><font color="blue"><b>&amp;axis</b></font></span>, Point="Point 1", Origin="My Origin", Project=Yes )</p>
<p>&#160;</p>
<p>In the above example the predefined parameters (<span style="color:#ff0000; font-weight:bold;"><font color="red"><b>&amp;frame</b></font></span>, <span style="color:#ff0000; font-weight:bold;"><font color="red"><b>&amp;axis</b></font></span>, <span style="font-weight:bold; color:#ff0000;"><font color="red"><b>&amp;x</b></font></span>, <span style="font-weight:bold; color:#ff0000;"><font color="red"><b>&amp;y</b></font></span>, <span style="font-weight:bold; color:#ff0000;"><font color="red"><b>&amp;z</b></font></span>) are initialised through the Get321Settings macro command. Their values are saved and used later by the commands Construct_Point and Construct_Transformation_321 (parameters marked in blue colour).</p>
